Because we recognize revenue and expense relating to monthly subscriptions and professional services over varying periods, downturns or upturns
in sales are not immediately reflected in full in our operating results.
As a SaaS company, under Accounting Standards Codification (“ASC”) 606, we recognize our subscription revenue monthly for the term of our contracts
and therefore a shortfall in demand for our software solutions and professional services or a decline in new or renewed contracts in any one quarter might not
significantly reduce our revenue for that quarter, but could negatively affect our revenue in future quarters. Accordingly, the effect of significant downturns in new
or renewed sales of our products and services might not be reflected in full in our results

